pr_body:
Fixes https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/issues/38637. Only helps with (de)serialization perf when the type of a property or collection element is `System.Object`.

- Avoids dictionary lookup during serialization for every element of a collection (if elements are all the same type).
- Avoids temporary creation of `MetadataDb` due to previous `Clone()` semantics.
- Avoids temporary array pool allocation\free for `JsonDocument`.
- Cached literal values for `True`, `False` and `Null` JSON values.
- Strings and Numbers avoid the temporary array pool and other allocs.

An issue [was created](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/issues/42755) to make the newly added `JsonElement.Parse(reader)` method public (currently internal).

Deserialize numbers:
- ~1.9x faster for string[1000], int[1000] and other number types.
- ~5.3x faster for bool[1000] due to caching of literal values.
- ~1.8x faster for objects (for a sample POCO).

Serialize numbers:
- ~1.4x - 1.6x faster for large collections.
- ~1.1x faster for objects (for a sample POCO).

